//! Cozette bitmap font, 6x13 monochrome, ASCII 0x20..0x7E.
//!
//! Kernel-side copy of the Cozette font also used by
//! `libcanvas::font6x13` in userspace. Regenerate both copies from
//! the same `.bdf` release via `tools/fontgen/bdf2rs.py`.
//!
//! Currently unused by the kernel framebuffer driver — the shutdown
//! and panic banners still render through `font8x8` because they are
//! large enough at 2x scale that the compact bitmap font would look
//! out of place there. Retained here so future kernel text (e.g. a
//! ring-0 debug console) can pick it up without reintroducing the
//! font tooling dependency in the kernel build.
#![allow(dead_code)]
//!
//! Source: https://github.com/slavfox/Cozette (MIT license).
//! Cell layout: 6 pixels wide × 13 pixels tall. Each row is a `u8`
//! where bit 0 (LSB) is the leftmost pixel and bit 5 is the
//! rightmost visible pixel; bits 6-7 are always zero.
//! Rows 0-2 are ascender/accent space, rows 3-9 are the main
//! x-height, row 10 is the baseline, rows 11-12 are the descender
//! area used by 'g', 'p', 'y', etc.

/// Cell width in pixels (advance width). Callers that laid out
/// text against `FONT_8X8` should switch to this constant to keep
/// their code portable across font swaps.
pub const CELL_W: usize = 6;

/// Cell height in pixels.
pub const CELL_H: usize = 13;

